fbuf: keel's virtio-vga ("-s N,fbuf,...,virtio=on[,3d=on]")

From keelOS (root/bhyve/patch-fbuf.py, its virtio-vga part only): with virtio=on the
device is also a virtio-gpu (pci_virtio_gpu.c: PCI ID 1af4:1050, BAR 2 the virtio
regions, BAR 3 MSI-X, BAR 4 the 3D memory window). BARs 0 and 1 and ramfb stay as they
are for the firmware and a guest without the driver; once the driver shows a scanout
that is the console's picture (VNC).

--- a/usr.sbin/bhyve/pci_fbuf.c
+++ b/usr.sbin/bhyve/pci_fbuf.c
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "debug.h"
 #include "console.h"
+#include "pci_virtio_gpu.h"
 #include "pci_emul.h"
 #include "qemu_fwcfg.h"
 #include "rfb.h"
@@ -115,6 +116,15 @@
